    "long_instructions": "##**PROTOTYPE – SC2 AI in Your Program · Who Am AI? project**\r\n**This version: Finished sample – teacher exemplar and calibration Sample A (Riley, strong)**\r\n\r\nA completed project at the target level, for teachers and for scoring practice.\r\n\r\n- `my_prompt` has a character, chosen facts (a `facts` variable), and a rule that keeps the secret: \"Never say the word [secret]. If asked your job, give a clue instead.\"\r\n- **Off-topic check (Job 3):** AI that picks from choices checks each question. Try \"What is 2 plus 2?\"\r\n- **Hint:** AI writes a hint about how the worker solves problems.\r\n- **Guess check:** the player types a guess and AI picks Yes / No / Not sure. A wrong guess gets AI feedback on how close it was. Try \"a farmer\", then \"animal keeper\".\r\n- An empty AI answer gets \"I didn't catch that.\"\r\n- Lab2 levels don't save exemplar code, so this sample is its own level.\r\n\r\n**All versions**\r\n- Starter, no image generation: [104027](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/104027)\r\n- Starter with image generation: [105336](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105336)\r\n- Finished sample (this level): [105337](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105337)\r\n- Calibration sample, middle: [105339](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105339)\r\n- Calibration sample, weak: [105340](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105340)\r\n- Prompt Helper (AI Chat level): [105338](https://levelbuilder-studio.code.org/levels/105338)\r\n\r\n**Open questions**\r\n- Two AI calls per question (question check + answer) take about 9 seconds. Is that too slow for players?\r\n- Should students see this sample before they build, or only at the end?\r\n- The \"AI sends nothing back\" branch can't catch a failed AI call (the game just waits). Request a \"when AI fails\" event?",
